! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHERE THE COUNTER LEAVES -- FALSIFIABLE PREDICTIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! BACKWARD, for printed p.169: it must leave its counter at
! exactly 220410.40, which is what THIS page's line 4 prints.  The
! survey's "220410.60" for p.169's last row is a garbled reading;
! if p.169's transcriber lands anything other than 220410.40 as
! their exit, one of the two pages is wrong and the place to look
! here is my 8 full words -- a full word misread as a half word
! loses exactly 32 bits.
!
! FORWARD, for printed p.171: line 32 is "B,KUNSTC" at 220427.00,
! a HALF WORD.  >>> THE COUNTER LEAVES THIS PAGE AT 220427.40. <<<
! And that value is ALREADY CORROBORATED from a page outside this
! block: PDF p.185 (printed p.178) line 38 prints
!
!     220765.00   220427.50 00   B,K STRGE  -STORE IN COMMUNICATION REGION
!
! and a plain B prints target+.10, so that routine's entry is at
! 220427.40.  (The OCR's NAME there is garbled -- the page itself
! prints KSTRG -- but its ADDRESS is good; see below.)
! So, as predictions that can be killed:
!
!   * p.171's first LOCATED row prints 220427.40.
!   * p.171's first label is whatever p.178's branch table calls
!     the routine at 220427.40.
!   * p.171's header opens a NEW card prefix, because deck JD's
!     routine ends on my line 32.
!
! (The survey's "220427.64" for PDF p.178 is consistent with a
! garbled ".40"; it is not treated as evidence either way.)
!
! >>> THE FORWARD HALF WAS THEN CHECKED AT 600 dpi, AND IT HOLDS --
!     TWO OF THREE EXACTLY, THE THIRD WITH A CORRECTION. <<<  PDF
!     p.178 was rendered for its HEADER AND ITS FIRST SEVEN ROWS
!     ONLY, LOCATION/NAME columns, NOT transcribed -- that page
!     belongs to another transcriber.  It prints:
!
!       header:  CARD ID KA000001 ... PAGE NUMBER  171
!       1*  2*  3*            banner, "*** STORE IN COMMUNICATION
!                             REGION ***"
!       4*  220427.40  *      SLC,$
!       5*  220427.40   000031.07 02   KSTRG   LCI,3,KQUANT
!       6*  220430.00   220431.03 01           LVI,1,$+1.0
!       7*  220430.40   220432.50 00           B,K CAB
!
!     So p.171's "SLC,$" prints 220427.40, which is IBM's own
!     assembler stating the counter arriving from THIS page, and it
!     is the value predicted above.  The join
!     p.169 -> 220410.40 -> THIS PAGE -> 220427.40 -> p.171 is
!     closed at the FORWARD end.  Only the backward end is open,
!     and only printed p.169 can close it.
!
!     >>> AND THE PREFIX CLAIM HOLDS: p.171 opens KA000001. <<<
!     So deck JD is exactly the 19 cards JD000001-JD000019 printed
!     on MY lines 14-32 -- the RIO routine and its banner, nothing
!     more.  FIVE consecutive one-routine decks are now known:
!     JA (p.168,
!     WAIT), JB (p.169, CHEX), JC (my lines 1-13, SIO), JD (my
!     lines 14-32, RIO), KA (p.171, STRGE).  TWO OF THEM FIT ON
!     ONE PAGE, which is the thing p.168 could not see.
!
!     >>> THE CORRECTION: THE LABEL IS "KSTRG", NOT "K STRGE". <<<
!     My prediction took the name from the VOLUME OCR of p.178's
!     branch table, which reads "B,K STRGE".  The page itself
!     prints "KSTRG" at 220427.40.  The ADDRESS the OCR gave was
!     right and the NAME it gave was not -- which is the workflow's
!     own rule about the volume OCR, demonstrated against me.  The
!     branch table's ADDRESS 220427.50 is still a second,
!     independent reading of where p.171 begins; its spelling is
!     not evidence of anything.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SYMBOLS DEFINED OFF THIS PAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every card below is the form the DEFINING page prints, or the
! stand-in convention the workflow requires.  No defining card is
! copied verbatim where copying would plant storage.
!
! S COMRG  215001.00  a STAND-IN, not a copy.  printed p.103 line
!                     8 DEFINES it as "SCOMRG XW,(8)520000." -- an
!                     XW is a PLACE, and copying it here would
!                     land a word at this page's own counter and
!                     refuse the body merge (printed p.157 did
!                     exactly that and had to undo it).  Only S L
!                     needs it.
SCOMRG  SYN, (8)215001.0
! S L      215001.04  printed p.103 line 14 DEFINES it, "S L
!                     SYN(BU,1),SCOMRG+0.04  -LEVEL OF INSTRUCTION
!                     COUNTER", and the dds (BU,1) is CARRIED --
!                     line 5's L and line 18's L take their LENGTH
!                     from the symbol, and line 28's BB does too.
!                     COUNTED BY ME: sixteen landed decks carry an
!                     SL card -- seven write "SCOMRG+0.04" as p.103
!                     does (p.147 among them), seven write the
!                     equivalent "(8)215001.04" (p.126, p.138,
!                     p.143) and two write "(8)215001.4", which is
!                     the same bit inside an octal literal.  This
!                     deck writes the DEFINING page's form.  LINES 5, 18 AND 28 PIN IT TO THE
!                     BIT.  The comment on lines 5/18,
!                     "-DETERMINE LEVEL OF IC", is the manual's
!                     "identifies the requestor by the status of
!                     the level bit (SL)" and the defining card's
!                     own "LEVEL OF INSTRUCTION COUNTER".
SL      SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+0.04
! S PROG S 215021.00  the program status table; printed p.109
!                     line 7 DEFINES it ("SPROGS DRZ(BU,64),2").
!                     A DRZ, so no dds is carried on a SYN -- deck
!                     p.168 writes exactly this card and the body
!                     image accepts it.  LINES 7 AND 20 CHECK THE
!                     HALF WORD.
SPROGS  SYN, (8)215021.0
! S SIO    000000.75  printed p.109 line 10 DEFINES it, "SSIO
!                     SYN(BU,1),.61  -SUPPRESSED MODE STATUS", and
!                     C22-6728-1 Appendix A tabulates "SSIO .61
!                     SIO bit.  If 1, the program is in SIO mode."
!                     Deck p.141 carries this card verbatim.  The
!                     dds (BU,1) is CARRIED: lines 8 and 21 write
!                     "(BU,1)" of their own, but line 21's comment
!                     "-TURN OFF SIO BIT" and the manual both say
!                     it is one bit.  0o75 = 61.  LINES 8 AND 21
!                     PIN IT TO THE BIT.
SSIO    SYN(BU,1), .61
! S TIC    215265.00  the STored Instruction Counter (C22-6728
!                     prose, "the saved IC is stored in STIC");
!                     COUNTED BY ME: twenty-six landed decks carry
!                     this exact SYN card.  LINES 10 AND 23 CHECK THE HALF
!                     WORD.
STIC    SYN, (8)215265.0
! S AS     000000.31  printed p.109 line 8 DEFINES it, "SAS
!                     SYN(BU,1),.25  -AUTO STACK STATUS".  0o31 =
!                     25.  LINE 24 PINS IT TO THE BIT, and its
!                     comment "-DETERMINE IF IN FIX UP" sits
!                     against the manual's "if the requestor is
!                     auto-stacked ... returns via KSUPP".
SAS     SYN(BU,1), .25
! S Q K    000000.40  printed p.109 line 9 DEFINES it, "SQK
!                     SYN(BU,18),.32", and C22-6728-1 Appendix A
!                     tabulates "SQK .32-.49  Interrupt queue
!                     count" -- eighteen bits, which is why the
!                     dds is CARRIED.  Deck p.141 carries this
!                     card verbatim.  LINE 25 PINS IT TO THE BIT
!                     (see WHAT THIS PAGE PINS).
SQK     SYN(BU,18), .32
! S TLR    215230.00  printed p.116 line 13 DEFINES it ("STLR
!                     DRZ(BU,64),29").  LINES 29 AND 31 CHECK THE
!                     HALF WORD.
STLR    SYN, (8)215230.0
! S LR PP  215266.00  printed p.116 line 18 DEFINES it.  LINE 29
!                     CHECKS THE HALF WORD, and prints the word
!                     printed p.168 line 22 prints -- that deck
!                     also cites printed p.123 line 43 for it, a
!                     claim INHERITED and not checked here:
!                     "215230.00 80 215266.36 20".
SLRPP   SYN, (8)215266.0
! S LR MCP 215362.00  printed p.116 line 26 DEFINES it.  LINE 31
!                     CHECKS THE HALF WORD, against printed p.168
!                     line 24's identical word.
SLRMCP  SYN, (8)215362.0
! K SUPP   216242.00  the service-op return routine, defined
!                     printed p.128; COUNTED BY ME, twenty-six
!                     landed decks SYN it here.  LINES 11, 24 AND 26 CHECK THE HALF
!                     WORD; the BIT offset stays unreadable.
KSUPP   SYN, (8)216242.0
! KUNSTC   222037.00  the unstack routine; C22-6728-1 names it in
!                     prose for THIS routine -- "control is given
!                     to the unstack routine (KUNSTC)".  Deck
!                     p.141 carries this SYN.  LINES 30 AND 32
!                     CHECK THE HALF WORD.
KUNSTC  SYN, (8)222037.0
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! lines 1-3 are the asterisk banner "**** SUPPRESS I/O INTERRUPT
! ****", three comment cards (JC000001-JC000003) emitting nothing;
! see WHAT COULD NOT BE SETTLED (E).
!
        SLC, (8)220410.40            ! line  4  printed "SLC,$" at 220410.40 *  SUBSTITUTED
KSIO    L(BU,1),SL,-18               ! line  5  printed "K SIC" / "S L"  -DETERMINE LEVEL OF IC
        LV,9,$L                      ! line  6
        V+I,9,SPROGS                 ! line  7  printed "S PROG S"  -PROG STAT TABLE FOR SL
        CM1111(BU,1),SSIO($9)        ! line  8  printed "S SIO($9)"
        V+I,2,.32                    ! line  9
        SV,2,STIC                    ! line 10  printed "SV,2,S TIC"
        B,KSUPP                      ! line 11  printed "B,K SUPP"
! lines 12-13 are two EMPTY comment cards (JC000012, JC000013),
! printing a bare "-" and nothing else; see (C).
! lines 14-16 are the asterisk banner "**** RELEASE I/O INTERRUPTS
! ****", three comment cards (JD000001-JD000003).
        SLC,$                        ! line 17  printed "SLC,$" at 220415.00 *  NOT substituted
KRIO    L(BU,1),SL,-18               ! line 18  printed "K RIC" / "S L"  -DETERMINE LEVEL OF IC
        LV,9,$L                      ! line 19
        V+I,9,SPROGS                 ! line 20  -PROG STAT TABLE FOR SL
        CM0000(BU,1),SSIO($9)        ! line 21  -TURN OFF SIO BIT
        V+I,2,.32                    ! line 22
        SV,2,STIC                    ! line 23  printed "SV,2,S TIC"
        BB,SAS($9),KSUPP             ! line 24  printed "BB,S AS($9),K SUPP"  -DETERMINE IF IN FIX UP
        LC,8,SQK($9)                 ! line 25  printed "LC,8,S Q K($9)"  -IF NOT, UNSTACK
        BXCZ,KSUPP                   ! line 26  printed "BXCZ,K SUPP"
        LCI,15,30                    ! line 27
        BB,SL,KMOVE                  ! line 28  printed "BB,S L,K MOVE"
        T,15,STLR,SLRPP              ! line 29  printed "T,15,S TLR,S LR PP"
        B,KUNSTC                     ! line 30
KMOVE   T,15,STLR,SLRMCP             ! line 31  printed "K MOVE   T,15,S TLR, S LR MCP"
        B,KUNSTC                     ! line 32
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING, as it stands on PDF p.177
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  1                                                                  -  ****************************************  JC000001
!   line  2                                                                  -  ********************SUPPRESS I/O INTERRUPT **************  JC000002
!   line  3                                                                  -  ****************************************  JC000003
!   line  4*  220410.40  *                                                      SLC,$                                      JC000004
!   line  5*  220410.40     215001.04 80  001067.20 50   K SIC   L(BU,1),S L,-18          -DETERMINE LEVEL OF IC            JC000005
!   line  6*  220411.40     000010.22 30                         LV,9,$L                                                    JC000006
!   line  7*  220412.00     215021.23 05                         V+I,9,S PROG S           -PROG STAT TABLE FOR SL           JC000007
!   line  8*  220412.40     000000.75 89  001000.36 F0           CM1111(BU,1),S SIO($9)                                     JC000008
!   line  9*  220413.40     000000.45 05                         V+I,2,.32                                                  JC000009
!   line 10*  220414.00     215265.05 30                         SV,2,S TIC                                                 JC000010
!   line 11*  220414.40     216242.10 00                         B,K SUPP                                                   JC000011
!   line 12*                                                                 -                                             JC000012
!   line 13*                                                                 -                                             JC000013
!   line 14*                                                                 -  ****************************************  JD000001
!   line 15*                                                                 -  -***********  RELEASE I/O INTERRUPTS  ***********-  JD000002
!   line 16*                                                                 -  ****************************************  JD000003
!   line 17*  220415.00  *                                                      SLC,$                                      JD000004
!   line 18*  220415.00     215001.04 80  001067.20 50   K RIC   L(BU,1),S L,-18          -DETERMINE LEVEL OF IC            JD000005
!   line 19*  220416.00     000010.22 30                         LV,9,$L                                                    JD000006
!   line 20*  220416.40     215021.23 05                         V+I,9,S PROG S           -PROG STAT TABLE FOR SL           JD000007
!   line 21*  220417.00     000000.75 89  001000.00 F0           CM0000(BU,1),S SIO($9)   -TURN OFF SIO BIT                 JD000008
!   line 22*  220420.00     000000.45 05                         V+I,2,.32                                                  JD000009
!   line 23*  220420.40     215265.05 30                         SV,2,S TIC                                                 JD000010
!   line 24*  220421.00     000000.31 89  216242.34 02           BB,S AS($9),K SUPP       -DETERMINE IF IN FIX UP           JD000011
!   line 25*  220422.00     000000.60 59                         LC,8,S Q K($9)           -IF NOT, UNSTACK                  JD000012
!   line 26*  220422.40     216242.30 42                         BXCZ,K SUPP                                                JD000013
!   line 27*  220423.00     000036.37 02                         LCI,15,30                                                  JD000014
!   line 28*  220423.40     215001.04 80  220426.34 02           BB,S L,K MOVE                                              JD000015
!   line 29*  220424.40     215230.00 80  215266.36 20           T,15,S TLR,S LR PP                                         JD000016
!   line 30*  220425.40     222037.10 00                         B,KUNSTC                                                   JD000017
!   line 31*  220426.00     215230.00 80  215362.36 20   K MOVE  T,15,S TLR, S LR MCP                                       JD000018
!   line 32*  220427.00     222037.10 00                         B,KUNSTC                                                   JD000019
!
! (THE ROWS ABOVE ARE WHAT THE DECK READS, NOT WHAT THE DRUM PUT ON
!  the paper.  Open round glyphs are everywhere in the BINARY OUTPUT
!  column; read at 900-1800 dpi, the ones that matter print:
!    line  9  "COCCOO.45 C5"     -> 000000.45 05
!    line 10  "215265.C5 30"     -> 215265.05 30   (line 23 likewise)
!    line 21  "001000.CC FC"     -> 001000.00 F0
!    line 22  "COCCOO.45 05"     -> 000000.45 05   (the CLOSED byte)
!    line 24  "COCCOO.31 89"     -> 000000.31 89
!    line 25  "COCCOO.60 59"     -> 000000.60 59
!    line 29  "215230.C0 80"     -> 215230.00 80   (line 31 likewise)
!    line 30  "222C37.10 C0"     -> 222037.10 00   (line 32 likewise)
!  Every one of those C's stands in an OCTAL field, where a C cannot
!  occur, or is settled by the same statement printed elsewhere --
!  see GLYPH CALLS.  Lines 5 and 18's "215C01.C4 80" is the same.)
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CHECKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!SYM KSIO   220410.40
!SYM KRIO   220415.00
!SYM KMOVE  220426.00
!CHECK 220410.40 | 215001.04 80 001067.20 50 | line  5 K SIO L(BU,1),S L,-18 -- .04 is S L at SCOMRG+0.04, pinned to the bit (printed p.103 line 14); no index so the first byte is 80; the second byte 50 is LOAD, the counterpart of printed p.168 line 8's STORE D0 against this IDENTICAL operand word 001067.20
!CHECK 220411.40 | 000010.22 30 | line  6 LV,9,$L -- 0o10 is word 8, the left half of the accumulator (C22-6531 Appendix A); .22 is 2J = 18 for J=9
!CHECK 220412.00 | 215021.23 05 | line  7 V+I,9,S PROG S -- .23 is 2J+1 = 19 for J=9, so S PROG S is checked to the HALF WORD only; the comment prints "-PROG STAT TABLE FCR SL" and FOR is the word
!CHECK 220412.40 | 000000.75 89 001000.36 F0 | line  8 CM1111(BU,1),S SIO($9) -- .75 is S SIO at .61 decimal, pinned to the bit (printed p.109 line 10); 89 is index $9; the connective word 001000.36 F0 is the one printed p.18 prints six times, and its CLOSED 0 is the control for line 21's open one
!CHECK 220413.40 | 000000.45 05 | line  9 V+I,2,.32 -- .32 DECIMAL is 0o40, plus 2J+1 = 5 for J=2; the byte prints OPEN here and CLOSED on line 22, the same statement in the same character positions one routine later
!CHECK 220414.00 | 215265.05 30 | line 10 SV,2,S TIC -- .05 is 2J+1 for J=2 and NOT S TIC's offset, so the symbol is half-word-pinned only; printed p.168 lines 7 and 34 print this identical word
!CHECK 220414.40 | 216242.10 00 | line 11 B,K SUPP -- a plain B prints target+.10, so this checks K SUPP's HALF WORD at 216242.00 and nothing below bit 32. A HALF WORD, so the counter reaches 220415.00, which is what line 17's printed SLC,$ says
!CHECK 220415.00 | 215001.04 80 001067.20 50 | line 18 K RIO L(BU,1),S L,-18 -- bit-identical to line 5, and THIS ROW'S LOCATION IS THE CHECK: line 17's "SLC,$" is written as "SLC,$" in this deck, so 220415.00 is the counter arriving from line 11 and not an asserted origin
!CHECK 220416.00 | 000010.22 30 | line 19 LV,9,$L -- the same half word as line 6, printed twice on one page
!CHECK 220416.40 | 215021.23 05 | line 20 V+I,9,S PROG S -- the same half word as line 7
!CHECK 220417.00 | 000000.75 89 001000.00 F0 | line 21 CM0000(BU,1),S SIO($9) -TURN OFF SIO BIT -- the second printing of S SIO's .75; the page prints "001000.CC FC", four impossible C's in an octal field and a byte whose low nibble is i2 = 0 (no second operand); line 8's CM1111 thirteen rows above prints the CLOSED control
!CHECK 220420.00 | 000000.45 05 | line 22 V+I,2,.32 -- the same statement as line 9 with a CLOSED byte, which is what settles line 9
!CHECK 220420.40 | 215265.05 30 | line 23 SV,2,S TIC -- the same half word as line 10
!CHECK 220421.00 | 000000.31 89 216242.34 02 | line 24 BB,S AS($9),K SUPP -- .31 is S AS at .25 decimal, pinned to the bit; 89 is index $9; K SUPP's 216242.00 prints as .34, BB's operation bits being 0o34 (printed p.168 line 13 prints .74 = 0o40 OR 0o34 for a .40 target, which is what fixes the construction)
!CHECK 220422.00 | 000000.60 59 | line 25 LC,8,S Q K($9) -- .60 is S Q K's 0o40 (= .32 decimal, printed p.109 line 9) PLUS 2J = 0o20 for J=8, so the symbol is pinned TO THE BIT; 59's low nibble is index $9
!CHECK 220422.40 | 216242.30 42 | line 26 BXCZ,K SUPP -- 0o30 is the XCZ indicator on a .00 target; printed p.168 line 12's BXVZ uses 0o31 the same way and prints the same byte 42, which is what makes the two mutually checking
!CHECK 220423.00 | 000036.37 02 | line 27 LCI,15,30 -- the datum 30 DECIMAL prints as 0o36 in the address field and .37 is 2J+1 = 31 for J=15; bit-identical to printed p.168 line 20
!CHECK 220423.40 | 215001.04 80 220426.34 02 | line 28 BB,S L,K MOVE -- the third printing of S L's .04 on this page; the target is this page's OWN K MOVE at 220426.00, so this row checks a label produced inside the deck
!CHECK 220424.40 | 215230.00 80 215266.36 20 | line 29 T,15,S TLR,S LR PP -- bit-identical to printed p.168 line 22 (p.168's deck also cites p.123 line 43; INHERITED, not re-checked); both symbols checked to the HALF WORD
!CHECK 220425.40 | 222037.10 00 | line 30 B,KUNSTC -- target+.10 on KUNSTC's 222037.00; printed p.141 line 38 prints the identical word
!CHECK 220426.00 | 215230.00 80 215362.36 20 | line 31 K MOVE T,15,S TLR, S LR MCP -- the same transmit against S LR MCP; lines 29 and 31 differ ONLY in the second address, which makes them each other's control. Bit-identical to printed p.168 line 24
!CHECK 220427.00 | 222037.10 00 | line 32 B,KUNSTC -- the same half word as line 30, printed twice. A HALF WORD, so THE COUNTER LEAVES THIS PAGE AT 220427.40, which is what printed p.171's first located row must print -- CHECKED at 600 dpi: p.171 line 4 prints "220427.40 *  SLC,$"
